      "text": "In order to solve for the problem, we will apply the tangent addition formula, which states that $\\tan (A + B) = \\frac{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}{1 + \\tan A \\tan B}.$\nTherefore, we have $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 + \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}.$\nSince $\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1,$ this simplifies to $\\frac{1 - \\tan x \\cdot 1}{1 + \\tan x \\cdot 1} = \\frac{1 - \\tan x}{1 + \\tan x}.$\nSince $\\tan x = 2,$ this simplifies to $\\frac{1 - 2}{1 + 2} = \\frac{-1}{3}.$\nTherefore, $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\boxed{-\\frac{1}{3}}.$The answer is: -\\frac{1}{3}",
