      "text": "Given, $\\tan x = 2$ and we want to find the value of $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right).$\n\nWe can use the formula for the tangent addition formula:\n\n\\[ \\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\cdot \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\]\n\nSince $\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1,$ we have:\n\n\\[ \\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + 1}{1 - \\tan x} \\]\n\nSubstituting $\\tan x = 2,$ we get:\n\n\\[ \\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2} \\]\n\n\\[ \\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{3}{-1} \\]\n\n\\[ \\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = -3 \\]\n\nReasoning Steps:\n1. Apply the tangent addition formula to the expression $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right).$\n2. Substitute $\\tan x$ into the formula.\n3. Substitute $\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1$ into the formula.\n4. Simplify the expression to find the value of $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right).$\n\nWe will implement the above steps in Python to verify the solution.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the known value\ntan_x = 2\n\n# Define the tangent addition formula\ntan_plus_pi_over_4 = (tan_x + 1) / (1 - tan_x)\n\nprint(tan_plus_pi_over_4)\n```\n```output\n-3.0\n```\nThe value of $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)$ when $\\tan x = 2$ is \\(\\boxed{-3}\\).",
